     "result_text_tail": "e retention. The pack has no 2027 new-customer plan, so the $0.8M is what new customers must add, not a forecast.\n- **Activation target:** I sized it on promotion customers churning like other SMB customers (2.1% a month), not on Customer Success's promise to halve churn. Halving would take SMB to 1.55%, below its level before the promotion.\n- **Enterprise +7% everywhere:** I applied 7% to all enterprise renewals, including uncapped ones. That keeps the plan simple but slightly conservative.\n- **The SMB price gate is my recommendation:** promotion churn near 2.1%, and no further fall in the 38% win rate against Inkwell.\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Errors:** the deck passes the skill's checks with no errors, and the layout check reports no overflow.\n- **One warning left:** the \"about three times\" churn multiple is written in words in the pack, so the script can't match it to a digit.\n- **Not previewed:** I couldn't look at the slides as images, because no slide viewer is available in this sandbox. Please flip through the deck once in PowerPoint.\n- **No web re-check:** all sources are the briefing pack, so there were no web pages to re-check.\n\nNext, I could switch the theme, or add a sensitivity slide showing how the growth bridge changes if SMB retention keeps falling.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- palisade-pricing-2027.pptx\n- palisade-pricing-2027-sources.xlsx (one sheet per content slide, plus live calculation formulas)\n\nThe deck spec and the script that builds it are in `./work/`."
